thread:
li: Quick heads-up — hit a subtle race between coroutine cancellation and our SDK retry wrapper while upgrading a large app to Kotlin coroutines. Can reproduce reliably on a Pixel 4 with a flaky network.

li: Symptoms: caller times out -> coroutine cancelled -> underlying OkHttp call completes on IO thread -> our retry wrapper sees a network error and retries, resulting in duplicate POSTs and two token refreshes.

maya: Which versions? Any stack traces?

li: Retrofit 2.9.0, OkHttp 4.11.0, kotlinx-coroutines 1.6.4. Minimal-ish stack: CancellationException bubbling from coroutine, then IOException from the retry wrapper depending on timing. I pasted a small repro gist on the issue.

carl: Classic race. The suspend adapter should cancel the Call via Call.cancel() but if the network thread wins and completes the response, the wrapper may observe success/IO exc depending on scheduling. We saw this before.

li: Repro snippet inside SDK wrapper: ```kotlin
suspend fun <T> retrying(callFactory: ()->T): T {
  var attempt = 0
  while(true) {
    try { return callFactory() }
    catch(e: IOException) {
      if (++attempt > 3) throw e
      delay(200L * attempt)
    }
  }
}
```

li: Problem: retrying() doesn't check coroutine cancellation and will retry after cancellation.

frank: Two short fixes: 1) make retrying check coroutineContext.isActive before delaying / retrying; 2) ensure suspend adapter cancels Call eagerly by using suspendCancellableCoroutine and invoking call.cancel() in invokeOnCancellation.

maya: Example change we used in the app: ```kotlin
suspend fun <T> retryingRespectCancellation(block: suspend ()->T): T = coroutineScope {
  var attempt = 0
  while(true) {
    ensureActive() // throws if cancelled
    try { return@coroutineScope block() }
    catch(e: IOException) {
      if (++attempt > 3) throw e
      ensureActive()
      delay(100L * (1 shl attempt) + Random.nextLong(50))
    }
  }
}

suspend fun <R> Call.awaitResponse(transform: (Response)->R): R = suspendCancellableCoroutine { cont ->
  enqueue(object: Callback { ... })
  cont.invokeOnCancellation { cancel() }
}
```

carl: Good. Also make token refresh single-flight (CompletableDeferred or Mutex) keyed by user id so duplicate refreshes won't happen even if retries slip through.

frank: We should add a lightweight SDK helper: suspendRetryRespectCancellation + suspendCallAwaitWithCancel. That will cover most mobile integrators and reduce footguns.

maya: Agreed. I'll open a PR with both helpers and a small unit test that uses a TestCoroutineDispatcher + fake okhttp to exercise the cancel->complete ordering. Will also add an emulator E2E test to CI.

li: Created issue: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk-android/issues/534 "kotlin: cancellation vs retry race causes duplicate requests and token refresh" (assigned to @maya).

devx-bot: New issue created: sdk-android#534 — "kotlin suspend: retry helper must respect coroutine cancellation" (assigned to @maya).

carl: Action items: 1) Add helpers (owner: maya), 2) Make token refresh single-flight and key by account id (owner: frank), 3) Add CI unit + emulator test for cancel race (owner: li).

li: Also adding a short note to mobile onboarding doc: "Use SDK suspend helpers or ensure retry wrappers call ensureActive() before retrying and cancel underlying Call on coroutine cancellation."

maya: Will include code snippet and link to the issue in the docs. Thanks all :thumbsup:
